Z||000006||Joe Torma||11-18-2001||04:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Joe Torma. Just the person I wanted to ask this to; Why in the blazes are popcorn and soft drinks so expensive in a theatre? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, it works like this, greedy movie companies set their price, and if we want the movie we have to deal with it...and make the money at the candy stand.<P>So, Warner Bros is money hungry and wants 70% of the ticket gross...this number usually decreases as the weeks go by...but not for this one.<P>Our tickets here are $7.00 SO...$4.90 to WB and $2.11 for us.  So far we've done $2502. $1751 for WB and $750 for us.  Payroll, electric, and heating are VERY expensive and we'd never survive...not that any theatre is doing well overall anymore.<P>Gotta make the $$$ somewhere.  Hey, I'm only a manager here-I don't set the prices!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Also, we are the offer cheapest movie ticket and candy around.<P><BR>||||reg||1
