Z||000016||The Fieromaster||11-18-2001||08:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pheagey:<BR><B>yes, Harry Potter must go! And with him Barney, the Telatubbies, Might morphinj power Ranger, Pokemon, etc etc etc...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree!! Harry potter is annoying the ****  outta me! I mean ok the trailer makes it look like the movie has GOOD graphics but whats up with the FREAKS dressing up like Harry Potter to go see the movie?? AND NO im not talkin about the little kids im talking about the 25+ year olds dressing up?????!!!!!??  OK Star Trek is ONE THING its OK to dress up for a Star Trek convention... its NOT right to be over like 30 and dress up for a Harry Potter movie!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000017||TRiAD||11-18-2001||08:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B> Can I borrow that stick when your done   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Triad, no flame taken, but I just think its insane that some Christians will protest a fantasy movie of this nature because its directed at kids.  I mean MUCH worse material moves through the media daily and you don't hear a peep, because its directed at adults... and you would have to be naive to belive that kids don't get their hands on "adult" material.<P>All Im saying is I cant understand it and it seems fanatical to me.  <BR>AND no flame intended</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No problem, I understand, and I'm not going to go out and organize a protest or anything,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BUT, children (and many adults  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) are VERY impressionable, and can only learn what we give them to learn from. From a Christian perspective, I try to raise my kids with the ideals outlined in the Bible, and witchcraft is <I>specifically</I> condemned. Yes, it's fantasy, but how many Wiccans do we have on here? At least 10? 25 years ago, there were almost NONE in the US. Yes, it's just kid's books/movies, etc, BUT, where do you think they get their ideas and beliefs?<BR>If it's something that's voulentary, and something that can be avoided, I let them see what it is, and explain to them why we're not going to be a part of it. I also give them a chance to complain, and ask questions, and answer any concerns they have. I also tell them, when they're older (they're only 9 and 14 months, this is all basically about the 9 yr old) that they can make their own decisions on these things, but as long as they're young enough that it's up to me, things will go this way. <P>Even though they promote this BIG time in school, she was very cool about it. <P>One last thought...<BR>If I wrote books about a child who was called of God, and could do miracles in His name (healings, resurrection, "challenges" of God, etc), the schools couldn't embrace it (it would probably be banned as religious material) and how many people do you think would go see the movie? Would there be 30 year olds dressed as the kid, or as Christ, going to see it?<BR>Witchcraft, fantasy or not, is a religion as well. Funny how they are not only allowed, but promoted in public schools, and embraced by the world. ||||reg||1
