Z||000021||frontal lobe||11-18-2001||11:35 PM||||cadaver, I'm not going to let you get away with that one without calling you on it.  25 years ago witches, satanists, wiccans, or whoever had to hide out in the closet for fear of Christians?!?!  Good one.  Try 250 years ago, not 25.  If you are going to stand by that, you are exposing yourself as a big whiner.<P>And just for correctness sake, 44 human writers that the Bible claims were directed by God, so ONE author.<P>I love the "extremist" name calling and the use of the word "rant".  You are exposing your bias against a certain belief system.<P>I'm NOT against any and all fantasy, but if the Bible specifically speaks against it, my kids and I can't have any part of it.  And for consistency that someone else wanted, yes, we basically can't go to ANY movies or watch 98+% of television.<P>Not ranting here, just giving an accurate, fair portrayal of a viewpoint.<P>And Mach10 and Neal--2 minute minors for both of you for high sticking.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But mainly I want Harry Potter to go away for SOCIAL reasons:  American's propensity to do anything to death.  Harry Potter happy meals, Harry Potter action figures, Harry Potter pajamas,  Harry Potter band-aids...||||reg||1
