Z||000024||2birds||11-19-2001||12:19 AM||||I just took my wife and kids to see the movie, and I thought it was pretty good.  Didn't even get the matinee price, and I don't mind at all.  Whole different animal from Barney, Teletubbies, Thomas the Tank Engine, or The Rockie and Bullwinkle Movie (been there, done that, fell asleep at the theater).<P>As far as freaks dressing up for the movie, just wait until The Fellowship of the Ring comes out.  All the pointy-eared, hairy-toed wierdos in the world will be out in force then.<P>With regard to Mr. Potter's movie, I don't recall a single reference, opposing or upholding to God, the Devil, the Bible, Koran, Talmud, or the Magna Carta in Harry Potter.  Plain old fashioned  good vs. evil.  And magic.  Don't see anything wrong with that.  Take a %!$%ing pill, OK?  Enjoy the movie.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Ken Wittlief||11-19-2001||12:33 AM||||the reviews are starting to come out on the movie - the one I saw said if you havent read the books you will not be all that impressed with the movie - the special effects are so-so, and you can tell that some of the more well know actors were on the set for about 2 weeks to get their sceans done, get their checks and be on their way.<P> BTW - why all the ragging on the popcorn prices? how much do you pay for a pizza at poppa johns or pizza hut? $10, $14?!<P> do you know how much it costs them to make a pizza? about a BUCK!<P> If the movie theaters want to make more money they should sell pizza or some reasonalble good food - then maybe people will go to the movies to eat and see a movie - or how about haveing a resturant at the movies?<P> how about coming up with some new snack like food that is good, can be a meal, and you can only get it at the movies?<P> I mean comeon - its not like we cant get popcorn when ever we feel like it.||||reg||1
Z||000026||DaRkLoRD||11-19-2001||12:44 AM||||I'm just going to say this once.<P>"satan" was created by the christian religion. Wicca is a much older religion, and THERE IS NO SATAN IN THAT BELIEF SYSTEM! I'm tired of seeing wiccans grouped with satanists, simply because the majority of christians don't understand what wicca is.<P>(p.s. I'm not wiccan, but my sister is, as are several of my friends.)<P>anyway.. back to Fieros.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
