Z||000030||Nashco||11-19-2001||02:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by onfire:<BR><B> This place is awesome. Me and a few friends went. Spent like $50, and we couldn't finish all the food. They serve beer and wine too. Very cool. I must say that there sound system wasn't exactly THX quality, but the beer made up for it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.cinemagrill.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cinemagrill.com/</A> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow, I'd never heard of that, even though I lived near Seattle for a long time.  That sounds like a cool place to check out, and I see they have one in Atlanta, not too far, cool.  Now, if I could only find a date! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000031||Formula88||11-19-2001||08:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dennis_6:<BR><B>How do you figure wicca is older than Christianity.  The Christian religion is the continuation of the Jewish religion.  Wicca is just a bunch of Satanic garbage period.  Figures the atheist would take up for any  religion but Christianity.  Same old lie nothing changes.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Because Wicca, and Pagan religions date back to the beginning of mankind.  Also, in certain paths of Wicca, there are numerous similarities and shared beliefs with Native American religion and Shamanism.  Are you saying Native Americans are all Satanists?<P>Remember, Satan exists only in the Christian doctrine.  Wiccans don't believe in a Satan.  How, then, can it be Satanic?<P>I'm not going to defend one religion over another.  Each person makes their own choices.  But if you intend to condemn a religion, at least take the time to find out what you're talking about.  Your argument makes as much sense as saying "Jews are all going to hell because they worship Spam."  It has no basis in fact and is simply a way to condem people who don't believe the same as you.<P>For anyone wishing to learn what Wicca really is, I suggest reading <B><I>"Wicca: A Guide to the Solitary Practitioner" </B>by Scott Cunningham.</I>  It's a nice little book that outlines the belief systems and some of the practices.  It's not an all encompassing "bible" of Wicca by any means.  There is no one source for info on Wicca or Pagan religions, as they are as varied as the different people of the world.  But, it's a good place to start.<BR>  ||||reg||7
Z||000032||JSocha||11-19-2001||09:26 AM||||<FONT SIZE="3"><B><I>FOOD FIGHT!</I></B></FONT><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000033||TRiAD||11-19-2001||11:57 AM||||Wicca does NOT go back to the dawn of man. <BR>Adam and Eve were the foundation of the Jewish/Christian nations. <P>Wicca IS old, but since Adam and Eve were aware of Lucifer, he can't be "newer" than Wicca. Heck, he's older than Christianity, being created himself before Man. <BR>Wicca itself has no "real" beginning. It is a mish-mash of SEVERAL Pagan religions that were blended as people became more mobile.<BR>...And just because you don't believe in Satan/Lucifer/whatever (which can be argued, but I won't) doesn't mean you're not "on his side". The Bible states that everyone who is not actively living in Christ is in opposition to Him, it doesn't mean you hold worship servces for him, it just means you are not a Christian. <P>I never said harry Potter said "go worship Satan". But you did hit it on the head. "Magic". That is sorcery, which is clearly in opposition to the Bible. <P>It's amazing how your misconceptions of Christianity are fine, but if anyone disagrees with you, we're suddenly ignorant of YOUR belief and need to go learn more about it. ||||reg||1
Z||000034||ray b||11-19-2001||12:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dennis_6:<BR><B>How do you figure wicca is older than Christianity.  The Christian religion is the continuation of the Jewish religion.  Wicca is just a bunch of Satanic garbage period.  Figures the atheist would take up for any  religion but Christianity.  Same old lie nothing changes.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>your total lack of understanding and tolerance for others belifes is typical of christians in regaurds to any others belife or religions.and shows why they are a danger to all others. call them the devil and then kill them like they did in the past.<BR>wicca is not satanic and is much older than judaio-christian belife.and less of a danger to nonbelivers.<P><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
