Z||000042||2birds||11-19-2001||09:45 PM||||Y'all folks are too serious.  Lighten up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My understanding of religion is that it is what you make of it, and we only answer to the Maker in the end, right or wrong, none of us can judge the other.  Is any of us here perfect?  Don't think so...<P>If fantasizing about a little magical fun and games is a sin, I think I can accept that, and any penalties involved.  My seven year old knows it (Harry Potter's world) isn't real, so why can't a bunch of adults get it, too?  If you don't want to see it, don't.  Boycott anything related, if you feel you need to.  <P>But don't tell ME that I can't take MY kids to see it, or that MY kid can't read the books and get credit for a book report about it.  I think that God (yes, I consider myself a Christian) gave me a brain and the ability to make my own decisions.||||reg||1
