Z||000718||maryjane||12-13-2001||12:25 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Triad: I wanna shot    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>In God We Trust. If Unca Sam calls you to war, isn't it your Christian duty? It appears as though that is what is accepted... Don't make sense to me neither    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Reply: Maybe I was right about my first impression after all.<P>It's stupid if you ask me. There are plenty willing to lay everything down WITHOUT making other people do so, too.<P>Reply: Wonder how many in the past layed down everything for your freedom, so you would have it to enjoy today? I'm sure glad they aren't alive to hear you say such a selfish thing. What a waste of their lives, to die for such a inconsiderate attitude.. Put any spin on it you want, you said it pretty clear.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Freedom is precious, I'd fight for yours, a complete stranger's in another land, for anybody's. Obviously, you wouldn't even fight for your own. Quite a sad commentary on your generation . Hope they aren't all as self-absorbed.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000719||TRiAD||12-13-2001||12:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Triad: I wanna shot   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>...In God We Trust. If Unca Sam calls you to war, isn't it your Christian duty?...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh, so being born in America makes you a Christian?! No, "political" or "patriotic" duties are NOT in anyway "religious" duties. Sorry...please try again, enjoy one of our lovely parting gifts. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>...Personal cost? Ostracization from his peers... Criminal proceedings... All the usual stigma associated with Draft-Dodgers. REGARDLESS of wether he showed up or not....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And there IS such a thing as "consciencious objectors". Last I checked, most of them were Christians though...funny how the atheists on the board think they were dodging and the Christians were who wanted us to fight the war. <P>Ray, your comments on the causes of the Vietnam conflict DEFINITELY give away your (lack of) age. Quit trying to be 50, I'd bet you're like 22, tops. NO ONE who was alive then (and I barely was) would think the war was about Christians fighting some other religion...<P>You too can enjoy one of our parting gifts, thanks for playing. <BR>||||reg||13
